me/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+7y=13 \\\\ -2x+5y=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+7y=13 \\\\ -2x+5y=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdb98914303911996d27ba6ad272178e6a8b8b2a5eaa5abf591d823574ec8381"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}13 & \\,\\,\\,4 \\\\ 19 & -2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}"] ["math" "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,13 & 7 \\\\ 19 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|}"] ["math" "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,2 & 13 \\\\ -4 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}"] ["math" "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}"] ["math" "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,7 & 13 \\\\ -5 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-77401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,1⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=k \\\\ x+4y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=5$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-7$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=13$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-77401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12+1 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-77401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdb98914303911996d27ba6ad272178e6a8b8b2a5eaa5abf591d823574ec8381"} {"question" "q-77401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-77401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-77401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-70252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+ky=-4 \\\\ 3x-4y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-70252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-70252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdb98914303911996d27ba6ad272178e6a8b8b2a5eaa5abf591d823574ec8381"} {"question" "q-70252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-70252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-70252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨-4,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9x+11y=-14 \\\\ 6x-ky=-34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=-4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 1 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- $-4|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ -4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdb98914303911996d27ba6ad272178e6a8b8b2a5eaa5abf591d823574ec8381"} {"question" "q-42613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-42613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,3⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}kx+3y=1 \\\\ 7x-2y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $-3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$\n- $3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=3|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdb98914303911996d27ba6ad272178e6a8b8b2a5eaa5abf591d823574ec8381"} {"question" "q-139979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,-2⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}15x+8y=-1 \\\\ kx+13y=-31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|=-4|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|$\n- $-2|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ -2|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdb98914303911996d27ba6ad272178e6a8b8b2a5eaa5abf591d823574ec8381"} {"question" "q-139980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "q-139980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "b090c311af001b48650e48fa09cbb7b89a2a10621168d246cf5215636c2c48b1"} {"question" "e-5230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/2d3571405367c6d4ce15927a1dbdb50a30af7d13580c7b9cd3c73bada0583c98.png)\nExpress $D_x$ in terms of a $2 \\times 2$ determinant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/example-5230.json" "file_sha256" "8a33b7873ca734af15789a1f1ccfc65fb26f4f990667f542c8fec415dadedc9f"} {"question" "e-5230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/example-5230.json" "file_sha256" "8a33b7873ca734af15789a1f1ccfc65fb26f4f990667f542c8fec415dadedc9f"} {"question" "e-4575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/example-4575.json" "file_sha256" "58a2e646ec910f506f69c581cbd4eee33f07a439aba96a9e295d54424217b03d"} {"question" "e-4575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/example-4575.json" "file_sha256" "58a2e646ec910f506f69c581cbd4eee33f07a439aba96a9e295d54424217b03d"} {"question" "e-4578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=4 \\\\ x+ky=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/b82f5c43c9ec788b95e7213bef63eb37e4abf9d0159f92cbeedc0f64c4d35283.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/648ce0c1b8b77c1230c6c634c676624f9c79c12ffc3942abc09d24d0fdc424d3.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/bc7a566778813050611b098cebe221aa77ac27677e922cd282fc8ff9c3670cfd.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/example-4578.json" "file_sha256" "ff7fb17243cf84ca77a32e7f1d7f3101006dd28ff00d916ee7218e11962b68a1"} {"question" "e-4578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\dfrac{D_y}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{36}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/example-4578.json" "file_sha256" "ff7fb17243cf84ca77a32e7f1d7f3101006dd28ff00d916ee7218e11962b68a1"} {"question" "q-42977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -46 \\\\ 6 & 20\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "36b77f802c09cfad0a6d20e7f75b005d33df5b186090203c4b53828101ca8245" "reviewer_session" "01a118ea-3923-70c2-acd9-0830602bde5f" "rationale" "Cramer's rule replaces the coefficient matrix's second column with the right-hand side (-46,20), retaining first column (-6,6). Thus Dy=det([[-6,-46],[6,20]])=156. Original option d (index 3) an