-6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{vmatrix}}$,\nwhere $D_{y} =$"] [17592186120374 :question/answer-fields 17592186118719] [17592186120365 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n${3x + 5y = 15; 2x - 3y =-9$.\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y =$"] [17592186120365 :question/answer-fields 17592186118665] [17592186119585 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n${x - y = 2; 2x + y = 1$.\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n$\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}$\nExpress $D_x$ in terms of a $2 \\times 2$ determinant."] [17592186119585 :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{x - y = 2; 2x + y = 1\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD &= \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{x} &= \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119526 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n${5x + 2y =-1; - 3x + 3y = 9$.\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants."] [17592186119526 :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{5x + 2y =-1; - 3x + 3y = 9\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{y} &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{D_{y}}{D} = \\frac{\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{vmatrix}}{\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{vmatrix}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119528 :question/problem "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below.\n${5x - 2y = 4; x + ky = 8$\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k$?\n\n1. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$\n2. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$\n3. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$"] [17592186119528 :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{D_y}{D}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{y} &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot 8 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 36\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{D_{y}}{D} \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{36}{\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}} \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} &= 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186118666 17592186118667 17592186118668 17592186118669 17592186118670 17592186118720 17592186118721 17592186118722 17592186118723 17592186118724] "immutable_fields" [[17592186118665 :answer-field/correct] [17592186118665 :answer-field/id] [17592186118665 :answer-field/key] [17592186118665 :answer-field/type] [17592186118719 :answer-field/correct] [17592186118719 :answer-field/id] [17592186118719 :answer-field/key] [17592186118719 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
